 641               /THIS ROUTINE DRAWS ANY ASCII SYMBOL ON THE PLOTTER.
 642               /IN ADDITION TO THE 63 ASCII SYMBOLS, THE CODES FOR 
 643               /CR AND LF ARE RECOGNIZED AND USED TO SIMULATE THESE
 644               /COMMANDS.  SYMBOLS ARE BASED ON A 5 X 7 GRID OF WHICH
 645               /4 X 6 IS USED SO AS TO PROVIDE SPACING.  SIZE 2 CHAR-
 646               /ACTERS ARE THUS .08" X .12" WITH .02" BETWEEN THEM.
 647               /LF MOVES .1" X SIZE BELOW THE PRESENT LINE, BUT IS EF-
 648               /FECTIVE ONLY DURING A SINGLE OUTPUT COMMAND AS THE PEN
 649               /IS ALWAYS RETURNED TO THE STARTING POSITION AT THE END.
